<Base title="Get Help" description="Current application status and proposed GEAR Moto Foundation program eligibility and recovery support.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Rider Support</div><h1>When the Road Changes,<br/><span class="accent">Community Matters.</span></h1></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><div class="program-callout"><strong>Applications are not open.</strong> GEAR has not opened a public gear, education, medical relief, or hardship grant application cycle. The information below summarizes proposed programs, not an offer or guarantee of funding.</div><h2>Which Program May Fit?</h2><p><strong>Gear</strong> is planned to help eligible riders obtain essential helmets and other protective equipment. <strong>Education</strong> is planned to support approved safety and riding courses. <strong>Assistance</strong> will guide riders toward appropriate resources and service providers. <strong>Recovery</strong> will house proposed accident-related medical and financial relief, rehabilitation and rebuilding support.</p><h2>Program Questions</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:gear@gearmotofoundation.org">gear@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for Gear, <a href="mailto:educate@gearmotofoundation.org">educate@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for Education, <a href="mailto:assistance@gearmotofoundation.org">assistance@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for resource guidance, or <a href="mailto:recovery@gearmotofoundation.org">recovery@gearmotofoundation.org</a> for general Recovery program questions. Applications are not open. Do not send medical records, financial documents or other sensitive materials to any of these addresses.</p><h2>Proposed Rider Relief Review</h2><p>The draft Recovery medical policy describes objective review of financial need, verified accident-related patient responsibility, relevant coverage, and accident circumstances. It proposes different review pathways for ordinary public-road accidents and lawful, organized, controlled track or training activities.</p><p>The draft also distinguishes ordinary riding mistakes from materially dangerous public-road conduct. Decisions would be internal charitable eligibility determinations, not legal findings of accident fault. A qualifying controlled motorsports event would not automatically be excluded merely because the activity involves performance riding.</p><h2>How Medical Assistance Would Work</h2><figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/images/motorcycle-crash-recovery-medical-bills-support.jpg" alt="Injured motorcycle rider reviewing medical paperwork at home with a supportive family member." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1672" height="941"/><figcaption>Recovery involves medical expenses, practical support and rebuilding after a crash. Illustrative image.</figcaption></figure><p>Potential eligible bills include verified deductibles, copayments, coinsurance, emergency care, rehabilitation, prescriptions and similar accident-related patient expenses. Direct payment to medical providers is preferred. The draft policy does not authorize unrestricted payment of an insurance plan's theoretical out-of-pocket maximum.</p><figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/images/gear-moto-foundation-rider-recovery-support.jpg" alt="Illustrative injured motorcycle rider reviewing recovery paperwork with a supportive companion." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1672" height="941"/><figcaption>Rider recovery and support, shown illustratively; no services or awards are depicted as completed.</figcaption></figure><h2>Privacy Comes First</h2><p>We are not collecting medical records or hardship applications through general email. Please do not email accident reports, insurance documents, financial records, health information or other sensitive materials. Secure intake procedures, final eligibility criteria, funding limits and application dates will be announced if programs launch.</p><p>For general questions about the developing Assistance program or available rider resources, contact <a href="mailto:assistance@gearmotofoundation.org?subject=GEAR%20Assistance%20Inquiry">assistance@gearmotofoundation.org</a>. Please do not send sensitive records by email.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="mailto:assistance@gearmotofoundation.org?subject=GEAR%20Assistance%20Inquiry">Ask About Assistance</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/programs/">Review Programs</a></div></div></section></Base>